{"type":"text","timestamp":1789191841876,"sessionID":"ses_f6bdd9542ffexaMJS7tzN21445","part":{"id":"prt_09424cefa001bQ8hw7e4U8Yw6F","messageID":"msg_09424c58a001BedZzVRYTcs9le","sessionID":"ses_f6bdd9542ffexaMJS7tzN21445","type":"text","text":"Done. Analysis complete and written to `/workspace/docs/jobs/sheet_mobile-notifications/tasks.md`.\n\n**Verification notes:**\n- Branch: worktree HEAD at `refs/heads/feature/sheet_mobile-notifications` — matches `brief.md`'s `branch:` field. (No shell available, so confirmed via `.git` worktree file.)\n- The previous analyst attempt stalled on a missing `docs/handover-mobile-notifications.md`; the current brief has been rewritten as fully self-contained (108 lines), so no handover doc is needed.\n- No render report / screenshots exist for this job, so no rendered ground truth was available.\n- Confirmed the prerequisites the brief claims already exist: `UserNotifications` store (`load`/`destroy`/`getUnread`/`markAllRead`), API routes (`list`, `read-all`), desktop `UserNotifications.svelte` bell + `Entry.svelte`, `nav.notifications` translated in all four i18n files, `setContext` in `+layout.svelte`. The only missing i18n key is the empty-state string.\n\n**Task breakdown (4 tasks, per the brief's priority order):**\n\n- **TASK-1** — New `/notifications` route page (load → markAllRead on mount, `Entry` rows with no-op `onClose`, `SubHeading` header, empty-state hint) + add `nav.notifications_empty` to `NavigationRecords` and all four i18n files. *Files:* `src/routes/notifications/+page.svelte` (new), `src/lib/types/translation.ts`, `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`. *Depends:* none. *Risk:* medium — async sequencing plus 4-file i18n sync; flagged a duplicate-`load()`/orphaned-visibility-listener note.\n- **TASK-2** — Bell row in the ⋯ overflow menu (hardcoded, next to settings/profile, not in `navItems`/`desktopOrder`), `'notifications'` → `bell` in `NavEntryIcon`, `urls.notifications`, `overflowOnlyItems` extension for active state, red dot on ⋯, unread-count badge on the bell row, and the polling lifecycle in `MobileNavbar`. *Files:* `MobileNavbar.svelte`, `NavEntryIcon.svelte`, `urls.ts`. *Depends:* TASK-1. *Risk:* medium — touches overflow active-state logic and adds app-wide polling to a persistent layout component.\n- **TASK-3** — `max-h-[calc(100dvh-8rem)] overflow-y-auto` on the ⋯ menu container (already overflows ~568px phones). *Files:* `MobileNavbar.svelte`. *Depends:* none (lands before/with TASK-2). *Risk:* low — CSS-only.\n- **TASK-4** — Optional polish: `Entry.svelte` renders a plain row when `notification.link` is null and makes `onClose` optional. *Files:* `Entry.svelte`. *Depends:* TASK-1. *Risk:* low.\n\n**Open questions resolved from the brief itself:** mark-all-read-on-open is the decided approach (desktop parity, recommended); the service-worker `notificationclick` fallback is explicitly out of scope (noted, not scheduled). No store or test changes are needed — the store already has everything and the changes are UI-only.","time":{"start":1789191835386,"end":1789191841873}}}
